---
import { ROBUSTNESS, PROSPECTIVE, ACTION_NAMES } from '../data/woven';
const recipe = [
  { n: '1', title: 'Select supervision by reasoning operation', text: 'To improve a downstream task, select supervision that teaches the reasoning operation the task requires, not supervision that matches its actions, scenes, or domains.' },
  { n: '2', title: 'Prefer large state changes for robustness', text: 'For robustness, prefer supervision with large state changes, such as object manipulation over camera motion.' },
  { n: '3', title: 'Supervise temporal and agent-driven tasks directly', text: 'Transfer does not cross the boundary between the temporal family and the other three, nor the boundary between passive physical events and agent-driven actions.' },
  { n: '4', title: 'Transition supervision helps transition tasks', text: 'For downstream tasks that involve no transition, such as static perception, transition supervision does not help.' },
];
const RMAX = 36;
const fMin = -1.5, fMax = 6.5;
const fx = (x: number) => ((x - fMin) / (fMax - fMin)) * 100;
const fmt = (x: number, d = 1) => `${x > 0 ? '+' : x < 0 ? '−' : ''}${Math.abs(x).toFixed(d)}`;
---
<section id="recipe" class="content-section">
  <div class="section-container narrow">
    <span class="section-tag">4 · Recipe</span>
    <h2 class="section-title left">A training recipe for visual world modeling</h2>
    <p class="lead">
      Controlled comparisons of the subsets yield four rules. Tested prospectively on held-out benchmarks, <strong>all five comparisons come out as the recipe predicts</strong>.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="section-container">
    <ol class="recipe-list">
      {recipe.map((r) => (
        <li>
          <span class="rn">{r.n}</span>
          <span class="rt">{r.title}</span>
          <span class="rx">{r.text}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <figure class="forest" aria-labelledby="forest-cap">
      <div class="frow fhead" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="fc">Comparison mixture</span><span class="fq">Questions</span>
        <span class="ftrack faxis">
          {[-1, 0, 2, 4, 6].map((t) => (<span class="ftick" style={`left:${fx(t)}%`}>{t > 0 ? `+${t}` : t < 0 ? `−${-t}` : '0'}</span>))}
        </span>
        <span class="fv">Δ [95% CI]</span><span class="fp">p</span>
      </div>
      {PROSPECTIVE.map((r) => (
        <div class="frow">
          <span class="fc">{r.comp} <small>rule {r.item}</small></span>
          <span class="fq">{r.set}</span>
          <span class="ftrack">
            <span class="fzero" style={`left:${fx(0)}%`}></span>
            <span class="fci" style={`left:${fx(r.lo)}%;width:${fx(r.hi) - fx(r.lo)}%`}></span>
            <span class="fdot" style={`left:${fx(r.d)}%`}></span>
          </span>
          <span class="fv">{fmt(r.d)} [{fmt(r.lo, 2)}, {fmt(r.hi, 2)}]</span>
          <span class="fp">{r.p}</span>
        </div>
      ))}
      <figcaption id="forest-cap">Accuracy of the mixture selected by the recipe minus each comparison mixture (points, mean over 8 seeds, 95% CI) on held-out benchmark questions.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <details class="more">
      <summary>Evidence for each rule</summary>
      <h3 class="sub-title">(1) The reasoning operation decides where supervision transfers</h3>
      <p>
        After removing the component shared by all transfer profiles, subsets teaching the same reasoning family have similar residual profiles (mean pairwise correlation <strong>+0.32</strong>),
        whereas subsets sharing only an action type are no more similar than subsets sharing neither (<strong>−0.22</strong> versus <strong>−0.23</strong>).
      </p>
      <figure class="wide-figure">
        <a href="figures/grouping.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="zoom-link" title="Open full-size image"><img src="figures/grouping.png" alt="Three correlation matrices of the 11 subsets' transfer profiles: raw profiles with all pairs positive; residual profiles ordered by action type with no block structure; residual profiles ordered by reasoning family with diagonal blocks." width="2400" height="673" loading="lazy" /></a>
        <figcaption>Correlation of the 11 subsets’ transfer profiles: raw (left), and residual ordered by action type (middle) or by reasoning family (right).</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h3 class="sub-title">(2) Larger state changes give more robustness</h3>
      <div class="robust" role="list">
        {ROBUSTNESS.map((r) => (
          <div class="rrow" role="listitem">
            <span class="rname">{ACTION_NAMES[r.s.split('_')[0]]}</span>
            <span class="rtrack"><span class="rbar" style={`width:${(r.d / RMAX) * 100}%`}></span><span class="rval" style={`left:calc(${(r.d / RMAX) * 100}% + 6px)`}>+{r.d.toFixed(1)}</span></span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="table-note">Gain on the state-perturbation test set (points over the base model): the four causal-dynamics subsets, then the passive-physical-event subset.</p>

      <h3 class="sub-title">(3, 4) Where transfer breaks</h3>
      <p>
        Temporal localization is learned only from temporal supervision: the four temporal subsets raise temporal-adjacency accuracy from 25.7% to 55.6–58.7%, while the other seven leave it near the baseline.
        The passive-physical-event subset contains no agent action and lowers accuracy on WorldPrediction (−10.2) and ActionEQA (−1.7). The 4 benchmarks of static perception and general video QA do not improve under any training.
      </p>

      <h3 class="sub-title">Prospective test</h3>
      <p>
        Mixtures of WOVEN items are composed before any training and evaluated on questions from benchmarks that played no part in deriving the recipe (MMSI-Bench, VLM4D, PhysBench, SPAR-Bench, MVBench, IntPhys 2, and CameraBench).
        The recipe mixture is compared with mixtures of the same size composed by matching the action (camera-heavy), by a different reasoning operation (temporal-heavy), by passive physical events (exogenous-heavy), or with no selection (uniform); each trains Qwen2.5-VL-3B-Instruct with 8 seeds.
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .recipe-list { list-style: none; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.4rem; margin: 1.4rem auto 0; max-width: 1100px; padding: 0; }
  .recipe-list li { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.35rem; }
  .rn { width: 28px; height: 28px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent-color); color: #fff; font-weight: 700; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .rt { font-weight: 600; color: #1c2a3a; line-height: 1.35; }
  .rx { font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.5; color: #444; }
  .robust { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; margin: 1rem 0 0.4rem; max-width: 860px; }
  .rrow { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 190px minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: center; gap: 0.7rem; }
  .rname { text-align: right; font-size: 0.9rem; color: #222; }
  .rtrack { position: relative; height: 22px; background: #f2f4f8; border-radius: 4px; }
  .rbar { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 3px; height: 16px; border-radius: 3px; background: var(--accent-color); }
  .rval { position: absolute; top: 2px; font-size: 0.82rem; font-weight: 600; color: #333; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .forest { margin: 2rem auto 0; max-width: 1000px; }
  .frow { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 170px 190px minmax(0, 1fr) 170px 60px; align-items: center; gap: 0.7rem; padding: 0.45rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #eef1f6; font-size: 0.88rem; }
  .frow:last-of-type { border-bottom: 0; }
  .fhead { font-size: 0.78rem; color: #667; font-weight: 600; border-bottom: 1px solid #d5dbe6; }
  .fc small { color: #778; font-weight: 500; margin-left: 0.25rem; }
  .fv, .fp { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; color: #333; }
  .ftrack { position: relative; height: 18px; }
  .ftrack.faxis { height: 16px; }
  .ftick { position: absolute; transform: translateX(-50%); font-size: 0.72rem; color: #778; font-weight: 500; }
  .fzero { position: absolute; top: -4px; bottom: -4px; width: 1px; background: #9aa3b2; }
  .fci { position: absolute; top: 8px; height: 2px; background: #1c2a3a; }
  .fdot { position: absolute; top: 3px; width: 12px; height: 12px; margin-left: -6px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent-color); border: 2px solid #fff; box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--accent-color); }
  .forest figcaption { margin-top: 0.8rem; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.5; color: #556; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .recipe-list { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .recipe-list { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .rrow { grid-template-columns: 130px minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .frow { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .frow .ftrack { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
    .fhead { display: none; }
  }
</style>
